        "subject": "LU-8622 tests: keep recovery-small 24b pages dirty",
        "message": "LU-8622 tests: keep recovery-small 24b pages dirty\n\ntest_24b writes to two files, has the OST evict the client\nand expects the eviction to discard the dirty pages, which\nprints the \"dirty page discard:\" warning it greps for. Both\nfiles can lose their dirty pages before the eviction lands,\nand the test then fails with \"no discarded dirty page\nfound!\". Janitor hits this on ZFS only, 163 times in 30\ndays.\n\nThe write that failed in test_24a leaves ar_force_sync set\non the whole OSC, so the first write here is done\nsynchronously and is never cached. The second file is\ncached, but writeback is free to flush it during the second\nor so it takes the eviction to reach the client.\n\nSpend one successful write to clear the forced sync i/o\ncarried over from test_24a, and stall OSC writeback for a\nfixed ten seconds, which outlasts the eviction. Convert the\nbare lfs and lctl calls in this test to $LFS and $LCTL while\nhere.\n\nFixes: 624a3ac23393 (\"LU-921 llite: warning in case of discarding dirty pages\")\nTest-Parameters: fstype=zfs testlist=recovery-small env=ONLY=24,ONLY_REPEAT=30\nTest-Parameters: testlist=recovery-small env=ONLY=24,ONLY_REPEAT=30\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I223f94482cade234529f756ea7657efb130ff705\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68844\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Jian Yu <yujian@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
